# The studio is a local authoring tool, not a page. It is in the repo so
# it is versioned alongside the blocks it builds against, which means the
# deploy carries it too — so it is closed at the edge. Nothing there is
# secret and it cannot reach anyone's disk over the network, but a
# CMS-shaped page on a portfolio is an invitation to go poking.
#
# Sent home rather than 404'd on purpose: this site has no 404.html, and
# adding one would change what every unmatched URL does, which is a much
# bigger change than hiding one folder.
#
# _redirects is read by the deploy, never by a local server, so the
# studio keeps working on localhost either way.
/studio        /   301
/studio/*      /   301
